  "body": {
    "id": "lem:exact-regret-path",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "For every \\(c>0\\) and \\(t=c/(1+c)\\), the causal penalized-welfare regret satisfies \\((1+c)\\sqrt n\\,\\mathscr R_n(c)=G(u_n,E_n)(t)=T_n(t)\\). Thus the interior process is an identified causal regret curve, and its values at \\(t=0\\) and \\(t=1\\) are defined by the two compactified limits.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "c",
      "t",
      "n",
      "Rreg",
      "G",
      "un",
      "En",
      "Tn"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:penalized-welfare",
      "def:oracle-learned-lotteries",
      "def:causal-regret",
      "def:compactified-path",
      "def:oracle-regret-path",
      "lem:bregman-identity",
      "ass:consistency",
      "ass:randomization"
    ],
    "justification": "This identity prevents the Gaussian path from becoming a detached statistical surrogate and pins every interior coordinate to the planner's causal objective.",
    "gap": "The presolve algebra and Fang--Ridder--Xie fixed-weight criterion motivate the identity, but the full local normalization and endpoint compactification are not a published result.",
    "consumer": "The simultaneous band can be interpreted directly in penalized-welfare units at every interior temperature selected measurably from the observed sample or the plug-in frontier.",
    "proof_tex": "Conditional randomization and consistency identify \\(\\mu_{n,ja}=E(Y\\mid X=j,A=a)\\); overlap makes each conditioning event positive.  In stratum \\(j\\), subtracting the action-zero mean, multiplying the objective by \\(\\sqrt n\\), and using \\(\\lambda_n(c)=c/\\sqrt n\\) gives\n\\[\n \\sqrt n\\left\\{\\sum_a\\mu_{n,ja}\\pi_{ja}-\\lambda_n(c)\\mathrm{KL}(\\pi_j\\|b_j)-\\mu_{n,j0}\\right\\}\n =(Ru_{n,j})^\\top\\pi_j-c\\,\\mathrm{KL}(\\pi_j\\|b_j).\n\\]\nThe Lagrange equations for maximizing the right side over the simplex are\n\\[\n (Ru_{n,j})_a-c\\{1+\\log(\\pi_{ja}/b_{ja})\\}=\\kappa_j,\n\\]\nand benchmark positivity gives the unique solution \\(q_{c,b_j}(Ru_{n,j})=\\pi^*_{n,c,j}\\).  For arbitrary \\(v,w\\in\\mathbb R^K\\), direct substitution of the Gibbs probabilities shows\n\\[\n \\big[v^\\top q(v)-c\\mathrm{KL}\\{q(v)\\|b\\}\\big]\n -\\big[v^\\top q(w)-c\\mathrm{KL}\\{q(w)\\|b\\}\\big]\n =c\\mathrm{KL}\\{q(w)\\|q(v)\\}=\\ell_{c,b}(v,w-v).\n\\]\nSet \\(v=Ru_{n,j}\\) and \\(w=R\\widehat u_{n,j}=R(u_{n,j}+E_{n,j})\\), sum with weights \\(p_j\\), and divide by \\(\\sqrt n\\).  This gives\n\\[\n \\sqrt n\\,\\mathscr R_n(c)=\\sum_jp_j\\ell_{c,b_j}(Ru_{n,j},RE_{n,j}).\n\\]\nMultiplication by \\(1+c\\), followed by \\(t=c/(1+c)\\), is exactly the interior definition of \\(G(u_n,E_n)(t)=T_n(t)\\).  The endpoint equalities are compactified limits proved in the hard- and high-endpoint lemmas; they are not additional observed-law definitions of the causal regret.",
